      "hints": [
        "Use part (a) to solve first for $\\sin^22\\theta$.",
        "Take both signs of $\\sin2\\theta$ and generate every $2\\theta$ for $0^\\circ<2\\theta<360^\\circ$, then halve."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the identity into the given equation $\\cos^4\\theta + \\sin^4\\theta = \\dfrac{5}{9}$:\n$$1 - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin^2 2\\theta = \\dfrac{5}{9}$$",
        "Isolate $\\sin^2 2\\theta$:\n$$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin^2 2\\theta = 1 - \\dfrac{5}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{9}$$\n$$\\sin^2 2\\theta = \\dfrac{8}{9}$$",
        "Take square roots:\n$$\\sin 2\\theta = \\pm\\sqrt{\\dfrac{8}{9}} = \\pm\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\approx \\pm 0.942809$$",
        "Find the principal angle in the range $0^\\circ < 2\\theta < 360^\\circ$:\n$$\\alpha = \\sin^{-1}(0.942809) \\approx 70.529^\\circ$$",
        "Determine the angles for $\\sin 2\\theta = +0.942809$:\n$$2\\theta = 70.529^\\circ \\implies \\theta \\approx 35.3^\\circ$$\n$$2\\theta = 180^\\circ - 70.529^\\circ = 109.471^\\circ \\implies \\theta \\approx 54.7^\\circ$$",
        "Determine the angles for $\\sin 2\\theta = -0.942809$:\n$$2\\theta = 180^\\circ + 70.529^\\circ = 250.529^\\circ \\implies \\theta \\approx 125.3^\\circ$$\n$$2\\theta = 360^\\circ - 70.529^\\circ = 289.471^\\circ \\implies \\theta \\approx 144.7^\\circ$$",
        "State all four solutions in $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\theta = 35.3^\\circ, \\quad 54.7^\\circ, \\quad 125.3^\\circ, \\quad 144.7^\\circ$$"
